WEBVTT

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:00.734
Hi.

00:00:00.734 --> 00:00:01.434
I'm Soya.

00:00:01.434 --> 00:00:06.027
I'm a cat, and I explain the things you keep hearing about.

00:00:06.027 --> 00:00:08.673
Today: what is a software factory?

00:00:09.973 --> 00:00:15.627
A factory makes the same kind of thing again and again, with steps you can check.

00:00:15.627 --> 00:00:18.907
A cookie factory goes: dough, bake, check, box.

00:00:18.907 --> 00:00:21.839
A software factory does the same for apps.

00:00:23.139 --> 00:00:24.541
Ours has five steps.

00:00:24.541 --> 00:00:27.417
One: read what is new in AI and software.

00:00:27.417 --> 00:00:31.835
Two: pick the idea that would help an everyday person the most.

00:00:33.135 --> 00:00:34.978
Three: build one small app.

00:00:34.978 --> 00:00:36.002
Four: check it.

00:00:36.002 --> 00:00:41.738
Tests, a scan for secrets, and a look at the phone screen, in English and in Hebrew.

00:00:43.038 --> 00:00:44.394
Five: ask a person.

00:00:44.394 --> 00:00:49.393
The factory sends a request that says, here is my change, please look.

00:00:49.393 --> 00:00:52.035
It is not allowed to skip the checks.

00:00:53.335 --> 00:00:54.483
Here is a trend.

00:00:54.483 --> 00:00:57.353
People now put an agent above the tools.

00:00:57.353 --> 00:01:01.586
It decides what is next, checks the result, and follows up.

00:01:01.586 --> 00:01:03.666
Some call that an outer loop.

00:01:03.666 --> 00:01:05.746
Our factory uses a small one.

00:01:07.046 --> 00:01:09.837
But an agent is only as good as its rules.

00:01:09.837 --> 00:01:15.352
Ours cannot spend money, cannot open accounts, and cannot promise anyone ownership.

00:01:15.352 --> 00:01:16.880
A person decides those.

00:01:18.180 --> 00:01:19.196
Why small apps?

00:01:19.196 --> 00:01:22.988
Because small things can be finished, checked and fixed.

00:01:22.988 --> 00:01:27.050
So the factory makes one app a day, until something catches.

00:01:28.350 --> 00:01:28.926
I'm Soya.

00:01:28.926 --> 00:01:33.598
Try the apps, tell us what you would add, and come back for the next one.

